  "new_commit_message": "fix(diagramming-code): drop the unused pre-analysis step and name a language in examples (#365)\n\nStep 1 told the model to build a QueryEngine and run engine.preanalysis()\n\"for data-flow diagrams\", but the diagram command builds its own engine and\nnever reads pre-analysis data: call-graph, complexity and data-flow output\nis byte-identical with and without it on Trailmark 0.5.0. Remove the step\n(one heredoc and one extra full parse per run), and drop diagramming-code\nfrom the core skill's \"always run preanalysis before\" sentence.\n\ndiagram.py defaults to --language python, so five examples without a\nlanguage parsed any repository as Python; add `-l auto`. The Quick Start\nfocused `main`, which fails on repositories without one; use a placeholder.\nA test keeps the skill's commands consistent with this.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: kz-tob <kara.zaffarano@trailofbits.com>",
